 "deepDive": {
  "domain": "Culture, media & sport",
  "title": "Who will run Kraków's 400m zł Music Centre?",
  "body": "Kraków's biggest new cultural building, the **Centrum Muzyki** (Music Centre) on ul. Piastowska near Cichy Kącik, is due to be handed over by the end of December 2026 and to open in spring 2027. Its foyer looks towards Wawel. It has a 1,049-seat concert hall, a 300-seat hall, rehearsal rooms and education spaces, and is meant to be home to the city's two orchestras, **Sinfonietta Cracovia** and **Capella Cracoviensis**. A resident at a public hearing put the total cost at about 400m zł.\n\nThe fight is over who runs it. The city development company **ARMK** wants to manage the building long-term and leave artistic programming to the orchestras. Both orchestra directors (Rafał Kokot and Jan Tomasz Adamus) want a cultural institution in charge. They fear it would otherwise become mainly a commercial rental venue, and they had said they would not move in under ARMK. In October, acting mayor Stanisław Kracik proposed giving the building to Sinfonietta. Mayor Łukasz Gibała [withdrew those draft resolutions](https://lovekrakow.pl/centrum-muzyki-lukasz-gibala-wycofa-uchwaly-i-zorganizuje-wysluchanie-publiczne) and called a public hearing, which was held on 5 November.\n\nThe money explains why it matters. According to [Kurier Krakowski](https://kk24.info/centrum-muzyki-w-krakowie-jeszcze-nieotwarte-a-juz-wywoluje-spor-w-tle-miliony-zlotych/), ARMK estimates running costs at about **15m zł a year** against 5-7m zł in revenue, plus about 7.5m zł for equipment. That lands on a city with nearly 9bn zł of debt and a mayor cutting the city paper Kraków.pl (2.5m zł) and association memberships.\n\nThe outcome so far is a stop-gap. The city [announced](https://krakow.pl/aktualnosci/344314,33,komunikat,centrum_muzyki_pod_opieka_armk_w_2027_roku.html) that 2027 will be a **transition year**: ARMK keeps the building, and the orchestras rent space, paid for with extra city grants. The land should pass fully to the city in early 2028.\n\n**What's next:** culture committee chair Mazurkiewicz's resolution asking that the centre go to cultural institutions, and Gibała's first 2027 budget (expected mid-November), will show how much the city will spend on culture. This week's cancelled concerts and shows during city mourning are a reminder of how central these institutions are to Kraków's public life.",
  "links": [
   {
    "label": "krakow.pl: Centrum Muzyki under ARMK in 2027",
    "url": "https://krakow.pl/aktualnosci/344314,33,komunikat,centrum_muzyki_pod_opieka_armk_w_2027_roku.html"
   },
   {
    "label": "Kurier Krakowski: costs and positions at the hearing",
    "url": "https://kk24.info/centrum-muzyki-w-krakowie-jeszcze-nieotwarte-a-juz-wywoluje-spor-w-tle-miliony-zlotych/"
   },
   {
